ntainer who follows the ledger will hit the sentinel gate. Related: the context-budget.py docstring still says \"This file also carries three decision probes\". Fix: reword removal_scope to name the summarization.py part and the canonical sentinel, and update the facade docstring. More generally, cond. 7 / the CHANGELOG do not say that script logic moved under _lib/** (context-budget, budget-summary, ceo-boot, audit-query, reality-ledger, profile-opus, …) is now sentinel-gated where the old script file was not. That is a tightening for adopters who patch these scripts, not a defect; worth one line in Known-open or in cond. 7.\n2. .claude/scripts/local/mac_sign_and_release.py:130 — the wrapper always passes --npm-readme-reviewed to `release.sh bump`. It only prints a prerequisite and never asks for confirmation. release.sh:58-62/561-570 makes this flag a deliberate human attestation, because the npm/README `last-reviewed` stamp is a tripwire. The wrapper turns that attestation into boilerplate on material a signed tag covers. Related nits:\n   - TRACK (line 16) and the \"Merge pull request #7\" message (line 113) are hard-coded.\n   - sign-merge always pushes main (line 119) without a --push opt-in, unlike cut-rc/cut-ga, while release.sh's header promises it never pushes.\n   Fix: require an explicit --npm-readme-reviewed (or an interactive confirmation) on the wrapper; parameterize the track and PR number; gate the main push behind --push.\n3. .claude/scripts/gen-command-skill-hook-map.py:206-219 — the generator takes the package to scan from the import (`from _lib._audit_emit_parts import install`) and ignores the `package=` keyword. For check_agent_spawn.py (install(..., package=\"_lib.agent_spawn\")) it scans _audit_emit_parts/*.py instead of agent_spawn/*.py. This does not change today's doc, because the facade itself matches. Also, the emitted \"Derivation rule\" text (line 352) still says \"source file\" although bound parts now count, and the strict utf-8 rea