{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7D9ZtsihUnFEVsKxjk5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LBWXGTEV2HLPErR9zxVzpS","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-149-model-id-allowlist.md","offset":740,"limit":70},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3086,"cache_read_input_tokens":148121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3086},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cf3be2a-1cec-4f25-9988-6f9e6658e555","uuid":"abdef10a-f65a-4079-9f1c-2ca1438397fb","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:07:18.920Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7D9ZekTNJjb8ciHqW5J","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LBWXGTEV2HLPErR9zxVzpS":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-149-model-id-allowlist.md","offset":740,"limit":70}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LBWXGTEV2HLPErR9zxVzpS","type":"tool_result","content":"740\t  live adapter's structured-output path sends a caller's `tool_choice` as\n741\t  given, and no caller outside the tests passes one (checked S357,\n742\t  2026-09-24). A caller that forces one on `claude-opus-5-5` gets that\n743\t  400; not changed here.\n744\t\n745\t### A3.5 What this amendment does NOT decide\n746\t\n747\t- Migrating any `veto_floor: true` agent file off `claude-fable-5`.\n748\t- `_lib/model_routing.py` `_ROUTING_TABLE` (debate/arch stay on\n749\t  `claude-opus-5`), the reviewer default in `check_codex_stop_review.py`,\n750\t  and the `hooks/_lib/tier_policy` `MODEL_ID` enum.\n751\t- Prices beyond the rate card (A3.1). The same derived patch gives the\n752\t  $4/$20 row to `cost-table.yaml` and to every cost-rollup table that\n753\t  `test_model_fleet_presence.py` binds to this ADR's working set, and\n754\t  0.05x to the two per-model cache-read tables that test holds equal.\n755\t  Per-model price tables outside that oracle (Owner-provenance snapshots,\n756\t  drift fixtures, research and tournament instruments, the tier-policy\n757\t  cost gate) are not changed. The rollups that look a model up by its\n758\t  exact spelling do not price the `[1m]`-tagged spelling of\n759\t  `claude-opus-5-5`.\n760\t- The `upgrade.sh` T3.4 gate that withholds the DirectoryAdded /\n761\t  Notification registrations from adopter settings: A3.2 item 11 raises\n762\t  the adopter floor to Claude Code 2.1.280 but leaves that gate OFF.\n763\t- `SPEC/v1/install-cli.md`: it lists neither `--allow-old-claude-code`,\n764\t  nor `--adopt-setting`, nor exit 6. Its exit-code table already lags the\n765\t  scripts (it stops at 3, while its own flag table names exits 4 and 5);\n766\t  the SPEC is not changed here.\n767\t- `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/team.md` and the CHANGELOG (closeout and release\n768\t  surfaces).\n769\t\n770\tThe A1.1 sentence on the primary session model and A2.2 item 4 are\n771\thistorical; the session pin is `claude-opus-5-5` (A3.2 item 4).\n772\t\n773\t## Amendment 4 — PLAN-176 semantic families (2026-11-01, Onda 6B)\n774\t\n775\tThe Owner authorizes family admission without a GPG ceremony for each model version.\n776\tThe earlier closed-list/per-bump clauses remain historical; this amendment replaces them.\n777\t\n778\t# MODEL_FAMILY_POLICY = \"semantic-families-v1\"\n779\t\n780\tThe explicit blocks remain deterministic compatibility mirrors. Their historic A2/A3 tail\n781\tis retained; new compatible identifiers do not need another entry or signature. Runtime\n782\tacceptance is explicit membership OR an anchored family: Claude opus/sonnet/haiku majors\n783\t4–9, GPT 5–9, o 3–9, Gemini 2–9, Grok 3–9. Only Opus, GPT and o families, plus the\n784\texplicit legacy floor, are VETO-eligible. Sonnet, Haiku, Gemini and Grok availability\n785\tdoes not grant a VETO seat. The retired `claude-opus-4-1` remains rejected.\n786\t\n787\t`_lib/model_currency.py` owns these predicates. The availability generator appends\n788\tmajor-family prefixes to the explicit IDs when this formal policy assignment is present,\n789\tso the harness segment-prefix matcher can select future family members without editing\n790\tsettings for each bump. Exact settings equality still compares against the generated\n791\tentries. A native availability prefix cannot express a per-ID retirement exception; the\n792\tretirement and VETO checks remain local guard policy. Acceptance validates local naming\n793\tand role policy, not provider availability, price, capability or a measured promotion.\n794\tThe preferred session model, fallback chain and role-to-provider assignments are unchanged.\n795\tChanges to families, floors or retirement rules remain policy changes; ordinary admitted\n796\tmodel versions require neither an ADR edit nor a per-version GPG ceremony.\n797\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cf3be2a-1cec-4f25-9988-6f9e6658e555","uuid":"e474d771-a69e-43f4-88cf-95136ac96ab9","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:07:18.937Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-149-model-id-allowlist.md","content":"  live adapter's structured-output path sends a caller's `tool_choice` as\n  given, and no caller outside the tests passes one (checked S357,\n  2026-09-24). A caller that forces one on `claude-opus-5-5` gets that\n  400; not changed here.\n\n### A3.5 What this amendment does NOT decide\n\n- Migrating any `veto_floor: true` agent file off `claude-fable-5`.\n- `_lib/model_routing.py` `_ROUTING_TABLE` (debate/arch stay on\n  `claude-opus-5`), the reviewer default in `check_codex_stop_review.py`,\n  and the `hooks/_lib/tier_policy` `MODEL_ID` enum.\n- Prices beyond the rate card (A3.1). The same derived patch gives the\n  $4/$20 row to `cost-table.yaml` and to every cost-rollup table that\n  `test_model_fleet_presence.py` binds to this ADR's working set, and\n  0.05x to the two per-model cache-read tables that test holds equal.\n  Per-model price tables outside that oracle (Owner-provenance snapshots,\n  drift fixtures, research and tournament instruments, the tier-policy\n  cost gate) are not changed. The rollups that look a model up by its\n  exact spelling do not price the `[1m]`-tagged spelling of\n  `claude-opus-5-5`.\n- The `upgrade.sh` T3.4 gate that withholds the DirectoryAdded /\n  Notification registrations from adopter settings: A3.2 item 11 raises\n  the adopter floor to Claude Code 2.1.280 but leaves that gate OFF.\n- `SPEC/v1/install-cli.md`: it lists neither `--allow-old-claude-code`,\n  nor `--adopt-setting`, nor exit 6. Its exit-code table already lags the\n  scripts (it stops at 3, while its own flag table names exits 4 and 5);\n  the SPEC is not changed here.\n- `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/team.md` and the CHANGELOG (closeout and release\n  surfaces).\n\nThe A1.1 sentence on the primary session model and A2.2 item 4 are\nhistorical; the session pin is `claude-opus-5-5` (A3.2 item 4).\n\n## Amendment 4 — PLAN-176 semantic families (2026-11-01, Onda 6B)\n\nThe Owner authorizes family admission without a GPG ceremony for each model version.\nThe earlier closed-list/per-bump clauses remain historical; this amendment replaces them.\n\n# MODEL_FAMILY_POLICY = \"semantic-families-v1\"\n\nThe explicit blocks remain deterministic compatibility mirrors. Their historic A2/A3 tail\nis retained; new compatible identifiers do not need another entry or signature. Runtime\nacceptance is explicit membership OR an anchored family: Claude opus/sonnet/haiku majors\n4–9, GPT 5–9, o 3–9, Gemini 2–9, Grok 3–9. Only Opus, GPT and o families, plus the\nexplicit legacy floor, are VETO-eligible. Sonnet, Haiku, Gemini and Grok availability\ndoes not grant a VETO seat. The retired `claude-opus-4-1` remains rejected.\n\n`_lib/model_currency.py` owns these predicates. The availability generator appends\nmajor-family prefixes to the explicit IDs when this formal policy assignment is present,\nso the harness segment-prefix matcher can select future family members without editing\nsettings for each bump. Exact settings equality still compares against the generated\nentries. A native availability prefix cannot express a per-ID retirement exception; the\nretirement and VETO checks remain local guard policy. Acceptance validates local naming\nand role policy, not provider availability, price, capability or a measured promotion.\nThe preferred session model, fallback chain and role-to-provider assignments are unchanged.\nChanges to families, floors or retirement rules remain policy changes; ordinary admitted\nmodel versions require neither an ADR edit nor a per-version GPG ceremony.\n","numLines":58,"startLine":740,"totalLines":797}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LBWXGTEV2HLPErR9zxVzpS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
