{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Exj4CgdHeeYUW2kFVKGuHs","type":"tool_result","content":"795\t  \"_model_pin_comment\": \"PLAN-163 T1.1 contingency (ADR-181 §Contingency) — session-default pin. CC 2.1.220 honors the top-level settings key \\\"model\\\" (zod: E.string().optional(); describe \\\"Override the default model used by Claude Code\\\"; source at 2.1.220 binary offset [REDACTED:rg], sha256 8addc857..., positioned between \\\"permissions\\\" and \\\"fallbackModel\\\" in the settings schema — NOT the internal workflow prop \\\"defaultModel\\\", NOT the env var ANTHROPIC_MODEL). Pinned to claude-opus-5-5 since ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357; Claude Opus 5.5 needs Claude Code >= 2.1.280); from ADR-181 until then the pin was claude-opus-5 (OQ1=b primary/fallback), which stays the fallbackModel. Rationale: APPENDING claude-sonnet-5 to availableModels makes the 2.1.220 tier-default (sonnet-5) an ALLOWED model, so enforceAvailableModels no longer redirects the session away from it and the session default would silently FLIP from claude-opus-4-8 (=availableModels[0], the prior fallback target) to sonnet-5; the explicit pin forecloses that flip. The pinned value MUST remain an EXACT member of availableModels below (claude-opus-5-5 is present): SessionDefaultPinTest in .claude/hooks/tests/test_template_dogfood_parity.py compares exact ids, while Claude Code itself admits an id that extends an allowed entry by a - segment and replaces a pin the allowlist does not admit with the default model at startup (with a warning). Env ANTHROPIC_MODEL / CLI --model still override per-session at runtime. Mirror this key in templates/settings/settings.base.json or SessionDefaultPinTest reddens.\",\n796\t  \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\",\n797\t  \"availableModels\": [\n798\t    \"claude-opus-4-8\",\n799\t    \"claude-fable-5\",\n800\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n801\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n802\t    \"claude-opus-5\",\n803\t    \"claude-sonnet-5\",\n804\t    \"claude-fable-5-1\",\n805\t    \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n806\t  ],\n807\t  \"_enforce_available_models_comment\": \"PLAN-153 wave-backlog (Anthropic ADOPT sweep 2026-07) — Claude Code >=2.1.202 verified semantics: when true and availableModels is a non-empty array, the DEFAULT model selection is also constrained to the allowlist (if the tier default is not in availableModels, Default resolves to the first allowed entry). ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357, measured on Claude Code 2.1.280): the harness matches availableModels entries by segment PREFIX (an entry admits every id that extends it by a - segment; claude-opus-5 already admitted claude-opus-5-5), so this key does NOT redirect a tier default that extends an allowed entry; the explicit top-level model pin is what fixes the session default. Schema-verified optional boolean, valid in project settings (cascade-trust mode). Caveat (Claude Code settings reference, read 2026-09-23): when an organization deploys ANY managed settings, Claude Code reads this key from the managed source alone and ignores it in this file — fail-open at harness level; acceptable because an availableModels list still gates explicit selection.\",\n808\t  \"enforceAvailableModels\": true,\n809\t  \"fallbackModel\": ["}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cf3be2a-1cec-4f25-9988-6f9e6658e555","uuid":"cbe56115-a760-4ba8-ada3-ff185432c93a","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:07:21.034Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/settings.json","content":"  \"_model_pin_comment\": \"PLAN-163 T1.1 contingency (ADR-181 §Contingency) — session-default pin. CC 2.1.220 honors the top-level settings key \\\"model\\\" (zod: E.string().optional(); describe \\\"Override the default model used by Claude Code\\\"; source at 2.1.220 binary offset [REDACTED:rg], sha256 8addc857..., positioned between \\\"permissions\\\" and \\\"fallbackModel\\\" in the settings schema — NOT the internal workflow prop \\\"defaultModel\\\", NOT the env var ANTHROPIC_MODEL). Pinned to claude-opus-5-5 since ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357; Claude Opus 5.5 needs Claude Code >= 2.1.280); from ADR-181 until then the pin was claude-opus-5 (OQ1=b primary/fallback), which stays the fallbackModel. Rationale: APPENDING claude-sonnet-5 to availableModels makes the 2.1.220 tier-default (sonnet-5) an ALLOWED model, so enforceAvailableModels no longer redirects the session away from it and the session default would silently FLIP from claude-opus-4-8 (=availableModels[0], the prior fallback target) to sonnet-5; the explicit pin forecloses that flip. The pinned value MUST remain an EXACT member of availableModels below (claude-opus-5-5 is present): SessionDefaultPinTest in .claude/hooks/tests/test_template_dogfood_parity.py compares exact ids, while Claude Code itself admits an id that extends an allowed entry by a - segment and replaces a pin the allowlist does not admit with the default model at startup (with a warning). Env ANTHROPIC_MODEL / CLI --model still override per-session at runtime. Mirror this key in templates/settings/settings.base.json or SessionDefaultPinTest reddens.\",\n  \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\",\n  \"availableModels\": [\n    \"claude-opus-4-8\",\n    \"claude-fable-5\",\n    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n    \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n    \"claude-opus-5\",\n    \"claude-sonnet-5\",\n    \"claude-fable-5-1\",\n    \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n  ],\n  \"_enforce_available_models_comment\": \"PLAN-153 wave-backlog (Anthropic ADOPT sweep 2026-07) — Claude Code >=2.1.202 verified semantics: when true and availableModels is a non-empty array, the DEFAULT model selection is also constrained to the allowlist (if the tier default is not in availableModels, Default resolves to the first allowed entry). ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357, measured on Claude Code 2.1.280): the harness matches availableModels entries by segment PREFIX (an entry admits every id that extends it by a - segment; claude-opus-5 already admitted claude-opus-5-5), so this key does NOT redirect a tier default that extends an allowed entry; the explicit top-level model pin is what fixes the session default. Schema-verified optional boolean, valid in project settings (cascade-trust mode). Caveat (Claude Code settings reference, read 2026-09-23): when an organization deploys ANY managed settings, Claude Code reads this key from the managed source alone and ignores it in this file — fail-open at harness level; acceptable because an availableModels list still gates explicit selection.\",\n  \"enforceAvailableModels\": true,\n  \"fallbackModel\": [","numLines":15,"startLine":795,"totalLines":980}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Exj4CgdHeeYUW2kFVKGuHs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
